The attached image displays a Western blot confirming the presence of secreted active IL-1β (17 kD) in the supernatant of dendritic cells. As contextualized by Figure 7D in the provided PDF, this blot verifies that the IL-1β measured by ELISA, particularly after priming with LPS and subsequent stimulation with Nano-11, is predominantly the active 17 kD form rather than the inactive 31 kD pro-IL-1β. Stronger 15 kD bands (representing 17 kD active IL-1β) are observed in the supernatant with Nano-11 treatment, intensified when combined with LPS, while the 30 kD pro-IL-1β is primarily found in cell lysates, particularly with LPS priming.